WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:06.500
Prioritization protects attention by deciding sequence, scope, and focus before work begins.

2
00:00:06.600 --> 00:00:11.400
It asks what matters most under constraint and what tradeoffs are required.

3
00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:19.420
Multitasking often hides costs through switching, attention residue, errors, unfinished work, and shallow progress.

4
00:00:19.520 --> 00:00:23.600
Activity can feel like progress even when outcomes are slowing down.

5
00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:26.520
Strong work systems make priorities visible.

6
00:00:26.620 --> 00:00:36.140
They limit active commitments, reduce open loops, protect focus, batch shallow tasks, clarify escalation paths, and use meetings carefully.

7
00:00:36.240 --> 00:00:39.280
They also match work to attention and energy.

8
00:00:39.380 --> 00:00:46.340
Demanding tasks deserve better focus windows when possible, while administrative work can often be grouped so it does not fragment the day.

9
00:00:46.620 --> 00:00:49.100
Prioritization is not a refusal to adapt.

10
00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:52.160
It is the basis for adapting responsibly.

11
00:00:52.260 --> 00:00:56.820
When new information appears, priorities can change, but the change should be explicit.

12
00:00:56.920 --> 00:01:01.400
If a new request matters more, something else may need to move.

13
00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:09.420
If WIP is full, the team should decide what finishes, pauses, or drops rather than pretending capacity expanded.

14
00:01:09.700 --> 00:01:11.860
The goal is not doing everything at once.

15
00:01:11.960 --> 00:01:16.040
The goal is doing the right work in the right order with enough attention to do it well.

16
00:01:16.140 --> 00:01:21.340
That is a calmer and more reliable standard than constant responsiveness.

17
00:01:21.440 --> 00:01:28.560
It supports better quality, clearer communication, fewer hidden commitments, and work that actually reaches completion.

18
00:01:28.660 --> 00:01:33.780
In practice, this means treating attention as a scarce resource every day.

19
00:01:33.880 --> 00:01:39.800
When the system makes choices explicit, people can move with more confidence and less reactive switching.
